      "raw": "<p>So I&#39;m playing the Sentinels in a PBF and in general I really like this deck - fun combos, great powers and the collection of lowest HP means it&#39;s usually an exciting ride. &nbsp;The one big hole is Writhe&#39;s signature card. &nbsp;It seems really, really lame whereas the rest of the signature cards feel pretty solid. &nbsp;For signature cards we have:</p><p>Dr. Medico - &quot;Hippocratic Oath&quot; - converts damage against villains to healing for friends + a per turn trickle heal. &nbsp;This can be some amazing healing if set up properly.</p><p>Mainstay - &quot;Durasteel Chains&quot; - -1 damage taken, +1 damage dealt. &nbsp;Only the fact that he is a &quot;mini&quot; character keeps this from being the best buff in the whole game (-1 damage is the whole deal for a whole host of cards for other characters). &nbsp;And getting the +1 damage is fairly easy as a lot of the cards are of the &quot;one of your heroes deals&quot; variety. &nbsp;Coupled with his base power and the card that redirects damage to him and he becomes a nigh inpenitrable shield for a turn.</p><p>Idealist - &quot;Aura of Vision&quot; - one player may draw a card. &nbsp;Who doesn&#39;t like more cards? &nbsp;This card makes Idealist Expatriette&#39;s best friend in the whole wide game. &nbsp;And it&#39;s free, no card play necessary.</p><p>And finally</p><p>Writhe - &quot;Caliginous Form&quot; - reduce damage to Writhe by 2, if any remains, redirect it. &nbsp;The dam red is nice, but I find that villain cards that target &quot;the third lowest&quot; hero target are rather rare, meaning you have to wait until reasonably deep in the game for this to be usefull and even then you have to do a fair amount of creative damage assigning to get this set up. &nbsp;Also, the dam red is significant enough that instances of damage that can be redirected are rare, making this card even less useful. &nbsp;(Although taking the dam red back off after redirect does make that redirect potentially very nice). &nbsp;I dunno, perhaps it&#39;s a balancing issue since so many of the deck cards are better with Writhe, but compared to the other signature cards this one seems very circumstantial.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Am I missing something?</p>",
