      "id": 128431,
      "name": "TheSoundOfTrees",
      "username": "TheSoundOfTrees",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/da6949/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-20T12:33:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It's a very effective card if facing \"damage all targets\" ennemies/environments, as it protects Writhe, and may lead him to \"highest\" HP fast - or keep him alive when an electropulse explosive goes full bang.</p><p>As you, I didn't like it at first, but I tend to use it more and more. It was the key card of end game in a lot of my recent games,especially in Vengeance settings, and in a memorable Matriarch fight. Most of the time it just is a DR 2 for Writhe, the Wraith's base power-like, but it often can be a very effective tool in end-game, if you manage to have him be the target of the most powerful attacks each turn. (Edit : especially with villains/envir that do retaliation damage during hero turns)</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
