      "id": 128432,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-20T12:44:58.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Interestingly, Cliginous Form is usually the second Signature I get out (with Durasteel Chains as the first).  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/sunglasses.png?v=9\" title=\":sunglasses:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":sunglasses:\"></p>\n<p>The damage reduction is huge, in general, helping to manage global damage. You are correct that, later in the game, this is far more effective, but it when it works it's really great. I've had more than a couple games in which Writhe was the highest-HP hero and was throwing the villain's damage back in their face - on the rare occasion when it got through the -3&nbsp;reduction (adding Mainstay's power to the mix).</p>\n<p>Honestly, Aura of Vision is often not very effective for me - for some reason, whenever I get it out, ongoing destruction immediately takes it away. Just my luck, I know, but - with one exception - that's been how it's played out.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/confused.png?v=9\" title=\":confused:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":confused:\"></p>\n<p>And Hippocratic Oath has usually (with the exception of Plague Rat) not worked out for me just due to cards not allowing him to do damage.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:03:12.245Z",
