      "created_at": "2015-01-20T20:17:58.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Koga\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/48/2058_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Koga:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>DrScott wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Writhe - \"Caliginous Form\" - reduce damage to Writhe by 2, if any remains, redirect it.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nActually the card says to redirect, <strong>then</strong> reduce by 2. So if 2 damage comes to him and he redirects it to something that has +1 damage taken then it will still do damage.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Actually, actually, here's the card text:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The first time Writhe would be dealt damage each turn, reduce that damage by 2 and redirect it to the villain target with the highest HP.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You reduce the damage by 2 and redirect it - there is no conditional, no separate timing, etc. You do both.</p>",
